    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0341" n="251" xml:id="pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5131/869: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in France (Marriner)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-30T15:00:00-05:00">September 30, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>345. From Ambassador Edge.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Re your 564, September 30, noon, no possible justification for French newspapers
                    to make such assumption. You may without qualification state that Ambassador
                    Edge is at the moment in Washington discussing details of French counter
                    proposal and full report which does not present insurmountable difficulties will
                    be in Embassy’s possession early next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
